setfield('REQ-fee-accounting-3','statement','Given a beneficiary with earned liability, when that beneficiary claims to a valid caller-selected destination, then only that beneficiary liability decreases and the hook makes one successful native ETH value call for exactly the claimed wei under the existing money-path guard. The destination may spend or forward ETH during execution; a final destination balance increase is not required as payment proof. A rejected value call or failed post-call solvency check reverts the liability debit and complete claim atomically. Zero and hook-self destinations remain invalid. Beneficiary-authorized destination overloads remain available. Overclaim, wrong caller, or reentrancy leaves every liability unchanged.','ERC20 balance-delta proof is invalid for a native recipient that forwards funds; successful guarded value transfer is the correct claim effect.')
setfield('REQ-fee-accounting-3','measurement','Claim tests cover equality and plus-one boundaries, historical beneficiaries, wrong callers, beneficiary-self and third-party destinations, contract recipients that retain or forward ETH, rejecting recipients, reentrancy, forced ETH, atomic rollback, and post-call solvency; process liability remains unavailable through beneficiary claims.','Keep claim authorization and rollback while changing only the native transfer proof.')
setfield('REQ-fee-accounting-5','statement','No external interaction on the active native ETH money path can reenter a money-moving path, retain a liability debit after a rejected value call, redirect another liability, or create funded liability from an unrelated or forced ETH balance. Native collection authenticates the exact PoolManager fee take; native payout executes the exact value under the existing guard and checks solvency after the call. The 10/40/250 basis-point cumulative accounting is unchanged.','Native calls replace ERC20 return-value and token-delta failure modes on the active release only.')
