setfield('REQ-launch-orchestration-2','statement','Given a completed provider graph launch, when the separate owner-signed seedCanonicalLiquidity transaction executes, then the payable call binds msg.value exactly to amount0Max in wei, native ETH is currency0, and Permit2 is used only for HKMN currency1. The existing launchAuthority caller and explicit payer refund destination are retained and need not be equal. After required HKMN approvals, read current slot0 immediately before mint and calculate exact native and HKMN debts using the pinned core TickMath and SqrtPriceMath rounding rules. Both debts must fit their maxima. PositionManager MINT_POSITION and SETTLE_PAIR receive only the exact native debt and mint the complete HKMN allocation into permanent custody. Refund exactly msg.value minus nativeDebt to payer; do not use PositionManager SWEEP, total hook balance, or a zero PositionManager balance assumption. Clear HKMN allowances atomically and refuse residual HKMN. Custody binds the minted token id only after owner, PoolKey, full range and liquidity verification. Existing or forced ETH cannot alter refund or liabilities. Before seed, HKMN remains restricted to the canonical market and the initialized empty pool cannot swap. A mint, settlement, refund or custody failure rolls back every seed-local effect while preserving the completed provider graph for an authorized retry.','Native seed needs exact value/debt/refund flow, not USDG Permit2 or balance-derived refund.')
setfield('REQ-launch-orchestration-2','measurement','Pinned real PoolManager/PositionManager tests compare exact debt rounding at boundaries and in-range prices; exercise insufficient/excess msg.value, native and HKMN maxima, existing/forced ETH in both contracts, distinct launch caller and refund payer, refund rejection, HKMN-only Permit2 cleanup, full allocation, exact range -887220 to 887220 at tick spacing 60, permanent custody, pre-seed swap refusal and graph persistence after failed seed substeps.','Exact native debt must be checked against real pinned manager behavior.')
